   "text": "You were a tiny bit of nutrient inside a dead grasshopper. Decomposers broke it down, and you went into the soil. You were raked into a compost bin with leaves and food scraps, and spread on the garden as compost. A plant's roots took you in. A grasshopper ate the leaf, and one day, you went back to the soil again.",
